/-
OnBytes/Shell/ProofToyFiles.lean: test data: the files of one test batch of the programs' tool, as Lean literals. Made by
a program and not meant to be read.

Source. blocks/frame/handover_proof.cpp of the programs' sources wrote them: a proof on the first table, with its request,
reply and claims, under two public files. The data are made-up toy data: no model and no weights; nothing in them is
secret. Of the key file only the first 232 bytes are stored: its head, the root and the record's eight answers, which is what
`toy-proof` reads of it. sha256 of the whole files:
  public-file-1.txt e7688b25e81080a2c35667fcd4a3b1d7bcc9154d8a1bf20fde03b6f1d38db962
  public-file-2.txt 747eed9005a7e13c42db595d00506b58734dfa2502c54ca28d12c53ac858a30e
